From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:24:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Port aurora-silicon/m1n1's merged change #47 (a07d8c86)

J713: hand the AOP over with its DAPF, firmware segments and windows

aurora-silicon/m1n1 #47 (erikwb/j713/aop-handoff), merged as a07d8c86,
ported as its merge diff against the first parent. It carries four
commits by Erik Bourget:

  b2cc18cd dapf: program the J713 AOP's T8132 DAPF bank with read-back
  50e294f0 kboot: hand the J713 AOP over with its DAPF, firmware segments and windows
  8d749003 docs: j713: the control DTB needs the AOP node for the AOP handoff
  1b9b611b dapf: coalesce the T8132 windows from the window that grew

The handoff only runs when the kernel DT asks for it (/chosen
linux-enablement-mac,dapf-handoff contains "/arm-io/aop"), only on a
board compatible with "apple,j713", and only while the AOP CPU is
halted. Any failed step disables the AOP node. So it fails closed (CODE:
dt_set_t8132_aop()). Nothing in this port has been booted.

docs/j713.md, src/dapf.c, src/dapf.h and both tests applied cleanly.

Conflict resolution, src/kboot.c: #47 builds on aurora-wip's
dt_set_aop_firmware(), which aaf9fe96 (T6040/T6041 AOP DRAM segments)
added together with its call in kboot_prepare_dt(). This tree has the
helper half of aaf9fe96 (previous commit) but not that function, so
git offered the whole aurora-wip function as new text against an empty
side. Resolution:

  - dt_reserve_t8132_aop_windows() and dt_set_t8132_aop() are taken
    unchanged from a07d8c86.
  - dt_set_aop_firmware() keeps #47's shape (find the AOP node by
    compatible, skip it unless it is okay, then dispatch to
    dt_set_t8132_aop()). It is gated to T8132 only and uses
    "apple,t8132-aop" only. aaf9fe96's T6040/T6041 branch is left out,
    because it would change T6040/T6041 behaviour, which is outside this
    lane.
  - The call goes in kboot_prepare_dt() right after dt_setup_sio(),
    where aaf9fe96/a07d8c86 put it.

The J713 values used here (16 DAPF slices in dart-aop instance 1, the
apple,j713 gate) are J713 values. A later commit converts the gate to
t8132_board_admitted(), and the J604 values go in the board-data table.

Fixture, tests/python/test_sio_reservation_full.py: it cut the SIO
helpers out of kboot.c up to "struct isp_segment_ranges {", which now
also takes in dt_set_aop_firmware(). The extraction is bounded at the
closing brace of dt_setup_sio() instead, taken unchanged from
aurora-silicon 6b00c5f4 ("tests: follow the merged kboot and NVMe code
in the host fixtures", #44), which made the same change for the same
reason.

Build (RELEASE=1 CHAINLOADING=1, clang/lld 23.1.4): no new warnings.

Hardware tested on: NOT YET
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
